const AI_TRANSFER_PERSONALITY = {
  // v89: AUCTION BUDGET & SPENDING STRATEGY OVERHAUL.
  // Root cause of conservative teams ending with 200-350M and aggressive teams
  // ending at 0-10M: the v88 dynamic-budget-planning system (getAuctionContext,
  // AI_TARGET_RESERVE, spendingPressure) was built but never actually wired into
  // the three live bidding call sites — they called aiSpendingLimit(team, item)
  // and computeAIBidDecision's getAIValuation with hardcoded empty queue/queueIndex,
  // so auctionProgress was always 0 and the spendingPressure/catch-up boost inside
  // aiSpendingLimit was dead code during real play. Separately, processAIBids and
  // computeAIBidDecision both throttled bid probability using flat hardcoded
  // thresholds (110/90/70) for EVERY personality, which fought directly against
  // the 5-20M / 25-60M / 50-100M target reserve bands — an aggressive team got
  // throttled at the same dollar figure as a conservative team, so aggressive AI
  // stopped competing far too early relative to its own much smaller reserve
  // target, while surplus cash was never pushed back into bidding. Together this
  // caused the late-auction competition collapse and left many lots uncontested.
  // v89 fixes:
  //   1. queue/queueIndex threaded through getAIValuation -> aiSpendingLimit,
  //      processAIBids -> aiSpendingLimit, and computeAIBidDecision -> both, so
  //      getAuctionContext's spendingPressure now actually engages live.
  //   2. Dynamic spending throttle in processAIBids/computeAIBidDecision now scales
  //      off each team's OWN target reserve minimum, not one shared hardcoded value.
  //   3. Added explicit Auction Pressure Scaling tiers at 50%/70%/85% completion
  //      (bid-chance and valuation multipliers), so late lots stay competitive.
  //   4. Added explicit Catch-Up Spending tiers at 100M/150M/200M+ cash-on-hand,
  //      applied to valuation, hard cap, and bid chance regardless of personality,
  //      so any team sitting on a pile of cash gets pushed to spend it down.
  // v87: Franchise Driver Strategy implemented. Each AI team now identifies a
  // preferred franchise target tier before the Driver Auction and reserves funds
  // specifically for securing at least one franchise-caliber driver. AI avoids
  // spending its franchise reserve on lower-tier drivers before its target tier
  // appears. Once a franchise driver is secured, aggressiveness drops significantly
  // on subsequent lots, preserving budget for constructors and tracks.
  // getFranchiseTier() maps budget→target tier; aiAvailableBudget() deducts a
  // per-tier reserve; getAIValuation() and aiSpendingLimit() both boost ceiling
  // for matching-tier lots and suppress it for lower-tier lots while reserve active.
  // v86: Dynamic spending thresholds raised (90→110, 70→90, 55→70) so AI starts
  // pulling back earlier in the auction, before reserves are nearly exhausted.
  // aiAvailableBudget constructor reserve raised 50→60 and track reserve raised 30→40
  // to better reflect real auction spend levels and widen the spendable-budget gap.
  // AI_MIN_REMAINING / AI_EMERGENCY_FLOOR raised 60→70 to give AI a fatter post-auction
  // cushion for Constructor/Track/Upgrade phases.
  // getAIValuation aggressive overpay factor reduced (1.05–1.08 → 1.03–1.05) to lower
  // individual bid ceilings without removing aggression from top-tier assets.
  // v85: processAIBids hardened with same dynamic-spending and emergency-floor guards
  // that computeAIBidDecision already uses. aiAvailableBudget double-reserve bug fixed.
  // runAITransferMarket starHunter threshold aligned to AI_MIN_REMAINING.
  // v84: Rebalanced to prevent aggressive AI from bankrupting itself in Driver Auction.
  // bidMultiplier lowered (1.35→1.20 aggressive, 1.15→1.10 balanced) to reduce overbidding.
  // overpayChance tightened (0.35→0.20 aggressive, 0.15→0.10 balanced) to preserve reserves.
  aggressive:   { bidMultiplier:1.20, starHunter:true,  overpayChance:0.20 },
  balanced:     { bidMultiplier:1.10, starHunter:false, overpayChance:0.10 },
  conservative: { bidMultiplier:0.90, starHunter:false, overpayChance:0.05 },
};

